---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Using Quilt Fabric Remnants in a Cutting Plan"
  description="Measure project-local fabric remnants as finite rectangles, allocate real cuts, and buy only the remaining shortfall."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Record physical pieces, not a stash total</h2><p>
      Two separate remnants cannot be treated as one magically joined area. Give
      each piece a width, length, quantity, and fabric identity.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Preserve useful leftovers</h2><p>
      A practical allocation should account for every placed piece and describe
      remaining rectangular regions without claiming they form one contiguous
      remnant.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use the right scope</h2><p>
      Check one rectangle with <a href="/calculators/pieces-from-fabric/"
        >Pieces from Fabric</a
      >. Reconcile several stock pieces and new fabric with the <a
        href="/fabric-cutting-planner/">project planner</a
      >; no permanent stash database is required.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
